{title: Christ the Lord Is Risen Today}
{artist: Charles Wesley}
{key: C}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune EASTER HYMN - Lyra Davidica (1708)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1739, tune 1708: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Christ the Lord is [F]risen to[C]day, [F]Al[C]le[G]lu[C]ia!
[C]Sons of men and [F]angels [C]say: [F]Al[C]le[G]lu[C]ia!
[C]Raise your joys and [G]triumphs [C]high, [F]Al[C]le[G]lu[C]ia!
[C]Sing, ye heavens, and [G]earth re[C]ply: [F]Al[C]le[G]lu[C]ia!
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Love's redeeming [F]work is [C]done, [F]Al[C]le[G]lu[C]ia!
[C]Fought the fight, the [F]battle [C]won: [F]Al[C]le[G]lu[C]ia!
[C]Death in vain for[G]bids Him [C]rise, [F]Al[C]le[G]lu[C]ia!
[C]Christ has opened [G]paradise. [F]Al[C]le[G]lu[C]ia!
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Lives again our [F]glorious [C]King, [F]Al[C]le[G]lu[C]ia!
[C]Where, O death, is [F]now thy [C]sting? [F]Al[C]le[G]lu[C]ia!
[C]Once He died our [G]souls to [C]save, [F]Al[C]le[G]lu[C]ia!
[C]Where thy victory, [G]O [C]grave? [F]Al[C]le[G]lu[C]ia!
{end_of_verse}
